  "upstream_semantics_changes": [
    "Fixed-register ranges are half-open; reject upstream one-past offset.",
    "Bounds/overflow checks before all firmware slicing and DMA publication.",
    "Firmware timeout stops further MCU submissions; hardware reset is required instead of submitting a patch-semaphore release on a possibly stalled DMA queue.",
    "Interrupt delivery stays disabled during this polling-only bring-up port.",
    "Firmware-ready state is not associated or connected state.",
    "RX groups, DMA length, raw management flags and TX_FREE token lists are checked before slicing/release.",
    "Legacy scan request requires explicit caller-approved channels; never selects full bands implicitly.",
    "Scan operation sequence namespace exhausts at127 instead of wrapping into stale completion identities.",
    "Transmit supports bounded unencrypted non-QoS three-address station ToDS/EAPOL frames; FromDS/WDS, QoS, fragmentation, protection and extra ordered headers fail before writes.",
    "Optional owner-generation validation runs before DMA RAM access and after coherency callbacks so copied rings reject retired backing leases; raw callers without a validator retain their borrowed-storage lifetime contract.",
    "Regulatory domain grants20MHz only, forces DFS NO_IR, rejects world/6GHz initiation and validates conducted-power ceilings from device/board authority.",
    "Rate power requires all161 caller-supplied signed half-dBm SKU entries and floors negative mBm without exceeding any conducted ceiling; no default calibration or permissive rate table is constructed.",
    "CLC validates older block/rule extents, selects actual EEPROM encapsulation and exact country, leaves future indices opaque and never silently falls back to world.",
    "Regulatory sessions pin their owner, preflight the entire policy before I/O, reject non-increasing generations/device epochs, and require independently proved reset after partial submission failure. The submitted stage does not imply firmware acknowledgement or RF readiness."
  ],
